A||N||3||bilbo||HIGH VOLUME OIL PUMP?||||5||
Z||000000||bilbo||01-08-2001||07:53 AM||||I was given a high volume racing oil pump a friend had ordered out of jc.jipme.My question is:I have a perfectly fine stock one but I want too start modifying my stock V6 should I switch or as they say"If it ain't broke don't fix it".Thanks ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Will||01-08-2001||10:48 AM||||The high volume oil pump will prolong the life of your V6 by keeping parts better lubricated than the stock pump.<P>Extra oil volume is good<BR>Extra oil pressure is BAD. Unless you're going to be revving WAY beyond the factory redline, put the stock pressure regulator spring from your stock pump into the new pump so that you maintain the same oil pressure you have now.<P>If you have access to machining facilities, there are a few modifications you can make to the pump to make it more effective. I can detail these if you would like.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Got2manyfieros||01-08-2001||10:59 AM||||The thing you have to watch with the high volume/high pressure pump is that the oil pump drive shaft is not a huge piece in the 2.8, and I know a fiero owner who has broken one using a bigger oil pump.  I don't think I have to explain why his motor promptly blew up.  ARP would probably make you a custom one if you called them up and told them what was going on (I'm pretty sure there is no aftermarket one available at this point).||||reg||1
Z||000003||bilbo||01-08-2001||11:22 AM||||Will-any info you can give me would be appreciated.Do you know if i can use the stock pick up screen off the old pump I was told this could create a clearence problem!!!!||||reg||1
